#: ../../../../../../home/insan/projects/sibuna/docs/book/operations.rst:975
msgid "HTTP routing by name and path"
msgstr "按名称和路径的 HTTP 路由"

#: ../../../../../../home/insan/projects/sibuna/docs/book/operations.rst:978
msgid ""
"An HTTP frontend selects a backend for each request, also for later "
"requests on one keep-alive connection and for each stream of an HTTP/2 or "
"HTTP/3 connection. The first matching route wins. A route gives a "
"``host`` or a list of ``hosts``, a ``path_prefix``, or both. We compare "
"host names without case or port and match a prefix of the normalized path "
"that ends at a segment boundary: ``/public`` covers ``/public`` and "
"``/public/x``, and not ``/public-admin``. A prefix that ends in ``/`` is "
"matched as written. Requests that match no route use ``default_backend``."
msgstr ""
"HTTP 前端为每个请求选择一个后端，同一个 keep-alive 连接上的后续请求，以及 HTTP/2 或 HTTP/3 连接的每个流也都如此。第一个匹配的路由胜出。路由给出 ``host`` 或一个 ``hosts`` 列表、``path_prefix``，或两者都给出。我们比较主机名时不区分大小写、不考虑端口，并匹配规范化路径中在段边界处结束的前缀：``/public`` 覆盖 ``/public`` 和 ``/public/x``，但不覆盖 ``/public-admin``。以 ``/`` 结尾的前缀按原样匹配。不匹配任何路由的请求使用 ``default_backend``。"

